   "widgets_values": [
    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - Prompt Enhancer (the third video tutorial)\n\nMOSS Prompt Enhancer: a prompt box that can also write the prompt, with MOSS-Image's own text\nencoder (Qwen3.5); no other model is loaded. The text preview shows what it wrote.\n  - as written: the idea is encoded as typed (what the first two videos used)\n  - caption: a paragraph that keeps to the idea (56-118 words in the video's tests)\n  - detailed: a photographer's or illustrator's brief (168-238 words). With no medium in the idea it\n    picks one: 8 of 9 tries chose an oil painting for this fisherman; write 'a photograph of' for a photo\n  - corrections: paste the detailed prompt back as the idea and add 'Corrections: ...' at the end (any\n    language). A hat and a cat: 6 of 6, the rest kept. Name what contradicts the change too: 'a young man'\n    kept the white beard; 'a young man with a short dark beard' worked 6 of 6\n  - detailed with an empty idea: a random prompt (the seed draws a medium, a subject and a place / time)\n  - layout: boxes for every element (see the Layout examples)\n  - tags (1boy, white beard, ...) are rewritten as prose; count tags are written as adults\nThe enhancer's own seed and temperature decide the text: same seed, same text; temperature 0 always\ngives the same answer. MOSS Latent's seed 1013 is the image seed of the videos.\n\nNegative: empty uses the official MOSS-Image negative. What you write is also told to the enhancer:\nwith 'hat', the six test captions said 'no hat' and no image had one (5 of 6 had one without it).\nAt CFG 1 (the turbo) the sampler does not use the negative itself.\n\nOptional (muted): Load Image. Unmute it (right-click > Mode > Always) to have the prompt written\nfrom the picture: with an empty idea the picture is the whole brief, otherwise the starting point.\n\nAbout 2 s per answer on an RTX 5090. Measurements: tools/RESULTS.md in the HaDeS MOSS Suite."
   ],
   "properties": {}
  }
